{
  "checked_at": "2026-10-28",
  "ruling": "D05 working draft (#329). Bob rules on D05; the rules below are encoded in lib/db/repositories/model-lifecycle.ts (MODEL_LIFECYCLE_RULES) so a ruling changes one constant and this file.",
  "rules": {
    "available": "available is true when the vendor's public API docs list the model id as callable on checked_at and the vendor has not deprecated it (basis api_docs), or when its open weights are downloadable on checked_at from the vendor's Hugging Face org (basis hf_weights). Preview-only, waitlist, consumer-app-only and restricted-access models are not available.",
    "major": "major is the integer generation the vendor markets; the tier line (line, tier) is a separate dimension. Point releases share a major: only the latest available point of each line and major is active.",
    "active": "Exactly one active row per line and major. An active row needs available true, an https availability source and a coding_source_url.",
    "deprecated": "deprecated is the archive: the row stays, keeps its URL and leaves the ranking. archive_reason is superseded (superseded_by names the active row that replaced it) or unavailable.",
    "coding": "coding_source_url names a page that lists the model in a coding benchmark. The Vals Terminal-Bench 4.0 page is the primary source. Only the URL is recorded; benchmark figures stay out of this file and load through the separate metrics step.",
    "scope": "Every model row of the seed files plus the live family rows named in MODEL_LIFECYCLE_LIVE_SLUGS. Image and video models are out of scope (D52)."
  },
